proposal:
  title: Nook Chat - Discord familiarity without Discord clutter
  status: proposed for review
  date: 2026-11-07
  companion: CHAT_INTEGRATION_PLAN.toon
  concept_image: NOOK_UI/chat/chat-concept.png
  image_fidelity: Concept shows composition rather than exact tokens; specification governs square corners and subtle selected backgrounds
  intent: Adapt Discord conversation hierarchy to Nook's existing social app and actual service contracts
  research_method: Official public Discord product references; local Discord app was not inspected because the desktop-control runtime was unavailable
  scope: Design only; no production components or backend changes
  example_data: Any names messages groups counts and avatars in concept images are fictional presentation data

references[3]{id,url,lesson}:
  desktop,"https://discord.com/blog/player-release-q12025",Readable density and clear channel context; avoid copying voice controls
  navigation,"https://discord.com/blog/refining-discords-mobile-experience-with-your-feedback",Keep people and groups discoverable together across desktop and mobile
  mobile,"https://support.discord.com/hc/en-us/articles/12654190110999-New-Mobile-App-Updates-Layout",Use conversation headers to reveal details without permanently occupying the small screen

direction:
  recommendation: One existing app rail plus one contextual chat directory; never add a second permanent server-icon rail
  reason: Nook already has navigation for Feed Search Chat Play Profile and Settings; another icon rail would compete with it
  borrowed: Stable channel context; left-aligned message timeline; restrained unread markers; contextual member details; persistent composer
  not_borrowed: Discord branding; purple accents; Nitro; voice controls; server boosts; dense toolbars; unsupported features
  terminology: Use Groups rather than Servers; use Members for group participants; use New message rather than Invite for a DM
  primary_screen: DM conversation is the first release; group channel is an extension of the same workspace

desktop_layout:
  app_navigation: Preserve expanded and collapsed sidebar behavior; collapsed rail stays 64px with centered 44px controls
  global_header: Preserve 64px app header with sidebar toggle and theme selector; no duplicated logout or theme controls inside chat
  directory: 280px target width; no drag-to-resize requirement in first release
  timeline: Flexible width with min-width zero; reserve at least 480px before offering a docked details panel
  details: Optional 248px panel only when chat workspace can fit directory plus timeline plus panel; otherwise use a modal Sheet
  width_policy: Judge available workspace width after the app sidebar; expanded sidebar must not squeeze the conversation into unreadable columns
  height_policy: Workspace fills remaining dynamic viewport height; directory and timeline scroll independently; composer remains in normal flex layout
  separators: Thin semantic borders between columns; no floating dashboard cards around every message
  default_details: Closed; opens through a labeled Members or Details button; closing returns width to the conversation
  header_alignment: Directory header and thread header both 56px high beneath the existing app header

directory:
  header: Chat heading and one New message icon button with tooltip and accessible name
  filter: Input labeled Filter chats; filters loaded DM peer names and group/channel names only
  filter_limit: This is not global people search and not message-content search; use the New message dialog to find people
  direct_messages: Upper section; 48px rows with 32px square avatar and peer display name plus username
  groups: Lower section; expandable named groups with letter-mark fallback; selected group reveals a flat channel list
  channel_rows: 44px rows with hash icon and channel name; no channel categories because no category model exists
  unread: Semibold name plus compact numeric badge where the backend provides unreadCount; accessible full count label
  active: Subtle orange background and 2px orange left edge plus aria-current; use readable neutral text in light mode
  footer: Quiet Create group action once groups ship; no duplicate account bar with microphone or headphones
  no_previews: Do not show invented last-message snippets or latest-message timestamps; backend list lacks them
  sorting: Deterministic alphabetic DM peer order as specified in the integration plan; channels keep API creation order
  group_unread: Do not invent group totals from summary data; show channel badges when their read-state endpoint has been loaded
  no_group_icons_api: Initials are presentation-only; no group avatar upload action without an endpoint

dm_screen:
  header_left: Square avatar; display name; username and Online Away Offline or Unknown text
  header_right: View profile action and Details toggle; no phone camera pin or message-search icons
  first_message_state: This is the start of your conversation with this person; small profile link and composer ready below
  details: Public identity summary and View profile; no email provider status mutual-group claims or invented activity
  presence: Use socket presence only; static profile status text is not a connection indicator

channel_screen:
  header_left: Hash icon and channel name; group name and truncated topic on a secondary line
  header_right: Members button with real fetched count; group/channel management menu where authorized
  timeline: Same renderer and composer as DMs; author identity displayed for each message group
  details_sections: About with group description and rules; Members with public identity and ADMIN or MEMBER labels
  member_navigation: Selecting a member opens their public profile; optional Message action uses the same DM creation flow
  membership_count: Derive count from loaded membership data; do not show a count while data is unknown
  admin_actions: Edit group; add member; change role; remove member; create edit delete channel; delete group
  member_actions: View details and Leave group; explain last-admin conflict instead of showing a dead end
  direct_add: Label the action Add member; clearly explain that it adds an existing user immediately rather than sending an invitation

timeline:
  alignment: All messages left aligned including the current user's; no alternating bubble layout
  message_header: 36px square avatar; medium-weight display name; subdued time; optional edited label
  text: 15px Inter with roughly 22px line height; plain text with preserved newlines and safe wrapping
  author_grouping: Consecutive same-author messages within five minutes may share avatar/header; break at date unread and deletion boundaries
  grouping_accessibility: Each message retains author and timestamp in its accessible representation even when visually grouped
  spacing: 16px horizontal padding on mobile and 24px on desktop; 16px between author blocks and 4px between continuations
  max_measure: Keep text readable rather than stretching sentences across a very wide monitor; do not add a card around the text
  dates: Centered date separator; timestamps use viewer locale with full date/time available accessibly
  unread_boundary: Labeled New messages divider based on confirmed read marker; omit if the boundary is not in loaded history
  own_actions: Small overflow menu appears on hover or focus; Edit and Delete only for own undeleted messages
  touch_actions: Provide a visible reachable overflow button on touch; long-press is never the only access path
  no_actions_toolbar: No reply reaction pin forward or bookmark controls without contracts
  deleted: Muted Message deleted tombstone; no remaining preview of deleted attachments
  failed_send: Pending row says Not sent with Retry action; retry refers to same frozen logical send
  older: Load older messages control at top; maintain scroll anchor; show retry in place on failure
  new_messages: If user is reading older history show a New messages jump control; do not force scrolling

composer:
  surface: One square bordered neutral surface inset 16px from thread edges
  content: Multiline input with Message this person or Message channel placeholder; visible accessible Send button
  send_button: Orange background with black text; 44px minimum target; disabled while current draft cannot be sent
  attachment_button: Paperclip control appears only when attachment milestone and storage gates are complete
  height: Start at about 52px; grow to about 160px then scroll internally; respect mobile safe-area inset and keyboard
  keyboard: Enter sends; Shift+Enter newline; IME composition does not submit; leave room for explanatory helper text
  draft_feedback: Character count near the limit; descriptive validation error; draft retained after network failure
  attachment_tray: Above input; square image thumbnail or PDF tile; uploading progress pending failed and remove states
  attachment_copy: Up to 5 files; 10 MiB each; JPEG PNG WebP GIF PDF; message text required
  stored_attachment: Neutral Attachment label unless authoritative filename metadata becomes available; image preview and explicit Download action
  no_fake_security: Do not display end-to-end encrypted or antivirus-scanned claims

dialogs[8]{name,fields_or_content,actions,contract_limit}:
  New message,Friends suggestions and debounced public people search,Open conversation,Exclude self; allow only what backend contact policy permits
  Create group,Name description rules,Create group,Creator becomes admin and general channel is created by backend
  Edit group,Name description rules,Save and Cancel,Admin only; no icon upload or public invite link
  Add member,Search existing users and show already-member state,Add member,Immediate membership rather than invitation
  Edit channel,Name and topic,Save and Cancel,Admin only; no private channel or permission overrides
  Member actions,Current role and permitted changes,Promote Demote Remove,Only ADMIN and MEMBER roles; last-admin conflict explained
  Delete confirmation,Name of target and effect on content,Cancel and explicit Delete,Group/channel deletion removes messages; leaving is separate
  Attachment preview,Permitted image plus Download and Close,Download and Close,PDF download only; expired URLs can be refreshed

responsive:
  desktop: Show directory and thread when remaining workspace width is at least 760px; details docks only above 1040px remaining workspace
  compact: Hide permanent directory when remaining workspace is narrower than 760px; thread header offers Back to chats
  mobile_home: Single Chat directory with the same DM and group sections; existing Nook navigation remains its drawer
  mobile_thread: Conversation fills content area; Back to chats at top; name/topic and Details control; composer at bottom
  mobile_details: Accessible Sheet with close button and focus trap; return focus to Details trigger
  mobile_channels: Group expansion reveals channels in directory; selecting channel enters thread; Back returns to prior group selection
  navigation: Preserve URL selection and browser history; no gesture-only navigation
  zoom: At 200 percent zoom switch to compact layout rather than horizontally scrolling columns

visual_system:
  dark: Black canvas; existing surface and raised-surface tokens for directory composer and details; light neutral text
  light: White canvas; light-gray contextual surfaces; near-black text; visible input boundaries
  accent: "#F16B3A"
  accent_rule: Reserve for active state send action unread marker and focus; small text stays neutral when orange lacks contrast
  shapes: Square panels buttons and avatar images; retain tiny circular presence indicators only
  avatars: Reuse AccountAvatar and its square boring-avatars pixel fallback; normalize local/provider URLs through existing helper
  documentation_drift: Existing design-system note permits circular avatars but current component and user preference are square; preserve the current component
  typography: Inter for labels and messages; existing monospace only for subtle metadata where useful
  atmosphere: Preserve shared orange-dot/glare identity in empty states and margins; use opaque reading surfaces behind message text
  motion: Subtle state transitions only; no moving particles beneath chat history; respect reduced-motion preference
  icons: Existing Tabler line icons at 20px for navigation and 16px for secondary metadata; no second icon library
  implementation: Existing shadcn Base UI Button Input Textarea Badge DropdownMenu Dialog Sheet Tooltip and Skeleton; reuse native scrolling

states[10]{state,presentation,action}:
  signed_out,Sign in to start a conversation,Log in
  empty_directory,Your conversations will appear here,New message
  no_selection,Choose a conversation or start a new one,New message
  empty_channel,Start the conversation in this channel,Focus composer
  loading,Restrained row or message skeletons,No fake unread count
  reconnecting,Small persistent Reconnecting banner,Keep history and draft visible
  failed_send,Inline Not sent row,Retry same logical send
  forbidden,You cannot contact this person or your permissions changed,Return to chats or refresh membership
  missing_thread,This conversation is unavailable,Back to chats
  session_expired,Sign in again to continue,Disconnect socket and clear private cache

service_fit[12]{feature,design_support,guardrail}:
  Direct conversations,DM list and New message flow,No fake last-message summary
  Message history,Chronological timeline and Load older,Respect legacy lookahead adapter
  Send retries,Pending and Failed rows,One request ID per logical send
  Edit and delete,Own-message overflow actions,Other clients refresh eventually until event contract exists
  Unread,Directory count and New messages divider,Not recipient read receipts
  Presence,Dot plus readable status text,Unknown when snapshot absent or connection lost
  Groups,Expandable named groups and details,No public discovery or server branding uploads
  Channels,Flat hash-prefixed list,No categories voice channels or permission overrides
  Membership,Member list and role-aware menus,Only ADMIN and MEMBER
  Attachments,Upload tray previews and download,Show only after HTTPS storage validation
  Search,Filter loaded chats and find people in New message,No message-content search
  Relationships,Friends suggestions and public-profile links,Friendship is not automatically a chat permission boundary

release_screens[7]{id,screen,milestone}:
  S1,DM directory with empty selection,DM core
  S2,Active DM with unread and send states,DM core
  S3,New message dialog with people search,DM core
  S4,Group channel with details panel,Groups
  S5,Group administration and member conflicts,Groups
  S6,Attachment tray preview and failure states,Attachments
  S7,Mobile directory thread and details in both themes,Every milestone

review:
  recommendation_to_approve: Unified directory and Discord-style message rows inside Nook's existing shell
  deliberate_omissions: Separate server rail; permanent member sidebar; fake previews; calls; typing; reactions; threads; custom presence setting; notification preferences
  next_step: Review DM and group-channel concepts before writing production components
  acceptance: Every visible control maps to an existing supported contract or a purely local presentation action
